# 🛡️ Trivy DevSecOps Security Scanning Project

An end-to-end, beginner-friendly **DevSecOps project using Aqua Security Trivy**. This project demonstrates how to scan application source code, dependencies, Docker images, Terraform files, and Kubernetes manifests for security issues — locally and automatically through GitHub Actions.

> **Training-lab notice:** The files under `examples/insecure/` intentionally contain insecure settings so Trivy can detect and report them. They are for scanning demonstrations only. Never apply or deploy these examples to a real AWS account or production Kubernetes cluster.

---

## 📌 1. Project Objectives

The objective is to integrate security scanning into the software development and deployment lifecycle (Shift Left Security).

By completing this project, you will learn to:

- Scan Docker images for OS and application dependency vulnerabilities.
- Scan source files and dependencies for vulnerabilities and exposed secrets.
- Identify misconfigurations in Terraform and Kubernetes YAML.
- Generate security reports in JSON and SARIF formats.
- Generate a CycloneDX Software Bill of Materials (SBOM).
- Automate security scans using GitHub Actions.
- Configure a security gate that can fail a pipeline when serious vulnerabilities are detected.

