## 🔍 8. Trivy Scanning Commands Explained

### A. Docker image vulnerability scan

```bash
# Scan the Nginx image
trivy image nginx:latest

# Display only HIGH and CRITICAL vulnerabilities
trivy image --severity HIGH,CRITICAL nginx:latest
```

Checks for known vulnerabilities in operating-system packages and application dependencies contained in the image.

### B. Filesystem scan

```bash
# Scan the current repository for vulnerabilities and secrets
trivy fs --scanners vuln,secret .
```

Checks supported dependency files and searches for exposed secrets such as credentials or tokens.

### C. Terraform and Kubernetes misconfiguration scan

```bash
# Scan the training examples for infrastructure misconfigurations
trivy config examples/insecure/
```

Examples of issues that may be detected include overly permissive network rules, insecure storage settings, privileged containers, and unsafe Kubernetes security settings. Exact findings depend on Trivy version and checks.

### D. Generate a JSON report

```bash
mkdir -p reports

trivy image \
  --format json \
  --output reports/image-report.json \
  nginx:latest
```

JSON is useful when another tool or script needs to process scan results.

### E. Generate a SARIF report

```bash
trivy fs \
  --scanners vuln,secret \
  --format sarif \
  --output reports/fs-results.sarif \
  .
```

SARIF is a standard format that compatible code-scanning platforms, including GitHub Code Scanning, can consume when repository features and permissions allow.

### F. Generate an SBOM

```bash
trivy image \
  --format cyclonedx \
  --output reports/nginx-sbom.cdx.json \
  nginx:latest
```

An SBOM (Software Bill of Materials) is an inventory of software components and dependencies included in an application or image.

### G. Configure a security gate

```bash
trivy image \
  --severity HIGH,CRITICAL \
  --exit-code 1 \
  nginx:latest
```

`--exit-code 1` makes Trivy return a non-zero exit status when findings match the configured severity filter. CI systems can use this status to fail a job.

